invariants	the invariant suite	2026-10-04T16:29:05.8988871Z     limit      the signature is the sources' own declaration, checked by nothing here: no tag is verified, no Rekor entry is looked up, and estate/verify/provenance/verify-provenance.sh records that this repository's own commits are not keyless-signed either. 'Signed' is therefore a property of the design, not an observation, and the word does no work until something verifies it.
invariants	the invariant suite	2026-10-04T16:29:10.9038153Z     limit      the consumer repositories are separate by URL and not yet by existence: estate/README.md describes a monorepo-style working tree whose top-level directories become their own GitHub repositories *at split*, and each up.sh rewrites the pinned URL to an in-cluster git server for the offline demo. The pins name real separate repositories; whether those repositories are live is a question this code does not ask.
invariants	the invariant suite	2026-10-04T16:29:10.9040534Z     limit      read from committed sources, not from a running cluster: this evidences what the repositories declare they consume, never that a control is in force right now. Whether continuous proof of force is required at all is build ticket 65's question and is still open.
invariants	the invariant suite	2026-10-04T16:29:10.9042289Z     limit      these pins are read from this tool's own repository (.estate-clone), not from any repository 'netflix' owns. The dependency block above evidences what THIS estate consumes; it names no pin, tag or repository belonging to the subject the proposal is about, and 'netflix' is not assumed to have an estate under Flux at all.
